    "media:imagetext": "Built by Donald McKay and launched in 1853 in East Boston, the clipper ship\n\"Great Republic\"\nwas the summit of achievement in the world of sailing ships.\nShe was, from the standpoint of size, appearance and cost... the King of Clippers.\n\"Great Republic\" was considered the largest, sharpest and most magnif-\nicent craft ever produced by any nation or age. Before\nshe had barely tasted\nRepubier, was a network of flames. She was tater rebuilt but with ser to Gage,\nsail plan and spars reduced.\nLike Pan Am's modern Clippers® of the air, the early clipper ships traveled the\nlanes of commerce to all far places of the world. Pan Am's Clipper fleet of the\nconsists of the\nfinest commercial\naircraft ever developed...\nand service.\nThis is\na faithful reproduction of an authentic Currier \u0026 Ives lithograph,\nrepro-\nduced through the\ncourtesy of the Mariners Museum, Newport News, Virginia.\nLITHO U.S. A.\n2001080,924",
