    "millsfield:images_texts": [
      "PAINTED BY J. P. BUTTERWORTH\nSonald Mo Kay Cog. Builter of the Leviathon\nCLIPPER SHOP «GREAT REPUBLIC\"\nLITH.\nRY NATIRRIED",
      "THE PRESIDENT SPECiAL\nBOiSSONS\nSherry\nDubonnet\nватракі\nVermouth Sec\nManhattan\nMartini\nBloody Mary\nScrewdriver\nWhiskey Sour\nTom Collins\nYodka\nCollins\nSootch\nBourbon\nGin\nCanadian\nYodka\nBeer\nNOTRE SELECTiON DES GRANDS VINS\nOUR SELECTION OF VINTAGE WINES\nVins de Bourgogne Tere de uvée\nVins de Bordeaux Grand Crû classé\nGREAT WINES OF BURGUNDY\nGREAT WINES OF BORDEAUX\nCampagne Brut Millésimé-Cuvée spéciale pour Pan American\nCHAMPAGNE SPECIALLY SELECTED FOR PAN AMERICAN\nCointreau\nДратвніе\nBénédictine\nCrime de Menthe Cognac VIP Benédictine et Brandy\nPOiSSON\nDuenelles de Pitondles Nantua\nQUENELLES OF SCALLOPS WITH SAUCE NANTUA\nENTREES\nFilet Mignon grille Maitre d'Hötel\nBROILED FILET MIGNON WITH MAITRE D'HOTEL BUTTER\nLigumes do Jardin, au beunne\nBUTTERED GARDEN VEGETABLES\nSautê d'Agneau au\nburry - Riz Pilaff\nI LAFF RICE\nDESSERT\nTartelette aux Truits\nFRUIT TARTLET\nCafe Américain\nThe Orange Pekoe\nAMERICAN COFFEE\nORANGE PEKOE TEA\nPAN AMERiCAN CUiSiNE BY MAXiM'S DE PARiS\n3703 0620",
      "Built by Donald McKay and launched in 1853 in East Boston, the clipper ship\n\"Great Republic\"\nwas the summit of achievement in the world of sailing ships.\nShe was, from the standpoint of size, appearance and cost... the King of Clippers.\n\"Great Republic\" was considered the largest, sharpest and most magnif-\nicent craft ever produced by any nation or age. Before\nshe had barely tasted\nRepubier, was a network of flames. She was tater rebuilt but with ser to Gage,\nsail plan and spars reduced.\nLike Pan Am's modern Clippers® of the air, the early clipper ships traveled the\nlanes of commerce to all far places of the world. Pan Am's Clipper fleet of the\nconsists of the\nfinest commercial\naircraft ever developed...\nand service.\nThis is\na faithful reproduction of an authentic Currier \u0026 Ives lithograph,\nrepro-\nduced through the\ncourtesy of the Mariners Museum, Newport News, Virginia.\nLITHO U.S. A.\n2001080,924"
    ],
